From: Alejandro Arrufat <15357691+AlexArrufat@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wpa_supplicant: preserve legacy PSK offload authorization

Rebase the existing Buildroot 2.11 compatibility revert onto 2.12.
The 2.12 update removes that revert, but upstream 2.12 still requires a
port-authorized event for PSK offload. Drivers such as brcmfmac need a
separate kernel fix before the revert can safely be removed.

Keep the old PSK compatibility behavior only. The OWE offload branch was
combined with PSK in 2.12; retain its authorization-event handling.

This preserves the behavior of the existing Buildroot 2.11 patch.
Kernel-side port-authorized reporting is the preferred long-term fix:
https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260912-brcmfmac-4way-handshake-offload-authenticated-event-v1-1-e41a6a8281a2@jannau.net

Upstream: Not applicable [compatibility with kernels lacking PSK port authorization events]
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Arrufat <15357691+AlexArrufat@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/wpa_supplicant/events.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/events.c
@@ -4921,10 +4921,18 @@
 		wpa_supplicant_set_state(wpa_s, WPA_COMPLETED);
 		eapol_sm_notify_portValid(wpa_s->eapol, true);
 		eapol_sm_notify_eap_success(wpa_s->eapol, true);
-	} else if (((wpa_s->drv_flags & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_4WAY_HANDSHAKE_PSK) &&
-		    wpa_key_mgmt_wpa_psk(wpa_s->key_mgmt)) ||
-		   ((wpa_s->drv_flags2 & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_OWE_OFFLOAD_STA) &&
-		    wpa_s->key_mgmt == WPA_KEY_MGMT_OWE)) {
+	} else if ((wpa_s->drv_flags & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_4WAY_HANDSHAKE_PSK) &&
+		   wpa_key_mgmt_wpa_psk(wpa_s->key_mgmt)) {
+		/* Preserve compatibility with drivers that complete the firmware
+		 * handshake before reporting association, but do not send a
+		 * separate port-authorized event.
+		 */
+		wpa_supplicant_cancel_auth_timeout(wpa_s);
+		wpa_supplicant_set_state(wpa_s, WPA_COMPLETED);
+		eapol_sm_notify_portValid(wpa_s->eapol, true);
+		eapol_sm_notify_eap_success(wpa_s->eapol, true);
+	} else if ((wpa_s->drv_flags2 & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_OWE_OFFLOAD_STA) &&
+		   wpa_s->key_mgmt == WPA_KEY_MGMT_OWE) {
 		if (already_authorized) {
 			/*
 			 * We are done; the driver will take care of RSN 4-way
